Citation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

IQ-TREE 2 is academic software and expects to be cited when used in published
work. This server drives it; it does not replace that obligation. If results from
this tool appear in a publication, cite IQ-TREE 2 — and the substitution-model
selection or bootstrap method actually used — as directed at
http://www.iqtree.org/, not this wrapper.

Author and institution details are deliberately not restated here. They belong to
the upstream project, which publishes its own current citation; a hand-copied
byline is exactly the kind of thing that goes stale or attributes the wrong
people.

